    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0740" n="690" xml:id="pg690"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-12-17"><hi rendition="#italic">December
                                17, 1893</hi></date>. (Received Jan. 6, 1894.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 139.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose the memorandum
                    of a conversation with his highness the grand vizier, yesterday, the 16th,
                    regarding the progress of the investigation of the outrage on Miss Melton. I
                    have attempted to keep you advised of the progress of this investigation on
                    account of the great interest felt in it by religious people in the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d698-a1.xml" xpointer="d698-a1"/>
